{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PS3 review PASS (LLM-Review +1); addressed its 3 advisory findings in PS4:\n- correctness: _revert_partial_fold now mirrors _rollback_fold's data-loss guard — the snapshot is removed only when every reverse-rename succeeded; a stuck *.retired source retains the snapshot as SNAPSHOT_INCONSISTENT for fsck --repair-snapshots (journal still discarded so recovery never revisits fsck territory).\n- tests: added unresolvable-HEAD indeterminate-branch test, recovery retain-guard test, and lock-unavailable defer-contract test (16 oracle tests total, all green).\n- mutation M8 (invert the recovery retain guard) confirmed KILLED. lint/typecheck/raw-git gate all green.\nAlso PS1 CI failure root cause: the raw-git-writes gate required inline \"# raw-git-ok:\" markers on the two git-reset call lines (fixed in PS3)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786686964567379001,"uuid":"6c99a04a-d08c-43ff-82af-c82978974e10"}